# Load cases in a table

A beam of span *L* under three load cases. The table takes the loads as input and works out each case's bending moment; the total row sums the columns. Its name, `Loads`, makes the columns available below as vectors.

```calc
L := 6 m
```

```table {name=Loads}
| Case    |        q [kN/m] |          M [kN*m] |
| ------- | --------------: | ----------------: |
| Dead    |             4.5 | = q*L^2/8 → 20.25 |
| Imposed |             7.5 | = q*L^2/8 → 33.75 |
| Wind    |             1.2 |   = q*L^2/8 → 5.4 |
| Total   | = sum(q) → 13.2 |   = sum(M) → 59.4 |
```

```calc
M_design := 1.35*M_Loads[0] + 1.5*M_Loads[1] = ? kN*m   #= 77.963 kN*m
```
